# MOONLIGHT VIGIL — the title screen.
#
# Two things about how this one is PLAYED, and the first is the one to read
# before adding anything to it.
#
#   THERE IS NO PAD, AND THE GAP IS THE POINT. This carried two square voices
#   holding the chord under the tune, and on a synth where nothing sustains a
#   bed has to be re-struck to be a bed — so they were, in turn: padHi on beats
#   1 and 3, padLo on beat 2. Three isolated attacks at two pitches is not a
#   texture, it is a TUNE, and what the title screen actually played was
#   HIGH–low–HIGH, gap, in every bar of the track. Both voices are gone rather
#   than re-spelled, because the room they leave suits a vigil: the bell
#   arpeggiates the chord in the intro, the pulse arpeggios carry it everywhere
#   else, and the bass has the floor. Anything that fills that space back in
#   has to earn it against silence, which is a high bar here.
#
#   THE TUNE STAYS ABOVE THE ACCOMPANIMENT. The flute sat A3–G4 once — the same
#   two staff spaces as the arpeggio's top — and the masked voice was the one
#   carrying the lament. An octave up is also where a breathy sine stops
#   sounding like a stopped organ and starts sounding like somebody humming.
#
# Compile:  node scripts/song-import.mjs content/songs/title.song --sheet

id     title
title  MOONLIGHT VIGIL
tempo  90
about
  A slow A-minor vigil in the 16-bit console tradition, and a sparse one: no
  pad holds the middle, so a breathy sine flute carries the lament an octave
  above a room with nothing in it but rippling pulse arpeggios and a plain
  triangle bass. A detuned square lead takes the relative-major chorus, and
  glassy echo bells keep watch through the breakdown. The harmonic language
  leans on the
  progressions classic game scores are built from — i–VI–iv–V verses, a
  I–V–vi–IV chorus lift — but the melodies are original; nothing is sampled
  or transcribed.

voice flute    sine vol=.042 gate=.95 attack=25 echo=.4 vib=5/18/250
voice lead     square vol=.03 gate=.92 attack=12 detune=6 echo=.3 vib=5.5/14/200
voice arp      square vol=.013 gate=.4 pan=.3 echo=.25
voice bass     triangle vol=.05 gate=.95
voice bell     sine vol=.024 gate=.5 pan=-0.4 echo=.55

section intro
  bell   a4*4 c5*4 e5*8 | .*16 | a4*4 c5*4 f5*8 | g#4*4 b4*4 e5*8
  bass   a2*16 | a2*16 | f2*16 | e2*16

section verse
  flute  e5*8 c5*4 d5*4 | c5*8 a4*8 | d5*4 f5*4 e5*4 d5*4 | b4*12 .*4
         e5*8 g5*4 e5*4 | f5*4 c5*4 a4*8 | d5*4 e5*4 f5*2 e5*2 d5*4 | b4*8 e5*8
  arp    a3 . c4 . e4 . c4 . a3 . c4 . e4 . c4 . | f3 . a3 . c4 . a3 . f3 . a3 . c4 . a3 . | d3 . f3 . a3 . f3 . d3 . f3 . a3 . f3 . | e3 . g#3 . b3 . g#3 . e3 . g#3 . b3 . g#3 .
         a3 . c4 . e4 . c4 . a3 . c4 . e4 . c4 . | f3 . a3 . c4 . a3 . f3 . a3 . c4 . a3 . | d3 . f3 . a3 . f3 . d3 . f3 . a3 . f3 . | e3 . g#3 . b3 . g#3 . e3 . g#3 . b3 . d4 .
  bass   a2*8 e2*8 | f2*8 c3*8 | d2*8 a2*8 | e2*8 b2*8
         a2*8 e2*8 | f2*8 c3*8 | d2*8 a2*8 | e2*8 b2*8

section chorus
  lead   e5*4 d5*2 c5*2 g4*8 | d5*4 c5*2 b4*2 g4*8 | c5*4 b4*2 a4*2 e5*8 | a4*8 c5*4 d5*4
         e5*4 g5*4 e5*4 d5*2 c5*2 | d5*4 b4*4 g4*4 b4*2 d5*2 | c5*4 a4*4 f4*4 a4*2 c5*2 | b4*8 g#4*4 e4*4
  arp    c4 . e4 . g4 . e4 . c4 . e4 . g4 . e4 . | g3 . b3 . d4 . b3 . g3 . b3 . d4 . b3 . | a3 . c4 . e4 . c4 . a3 . c4 . e4 . c4 . | f3 . a3 . c4 . a3 . f3 . a3 . c4 . a3 .
         c4 . e4 . g4 . e4 . c4 . e4 . g4 . e4 . | g3 . b3 . d4 . b3 . g3 . b3 . d4 . b3 . | f3 . a3 . c4 . a3 . f3 . a3 . c4 . a3 . | e3 . g#3 . b3 . g#3 . e3 . g#3 . b3 . g#3 .
  bass   c3*4 c3*4 g2*4 c3*4 | g2*4 g2*4 d3*4 g2*4 | a2*4 a2*4 e2*4 a2*4 | f2*4 f2*4 c3*4 f2*4
         c3*4 c3*4 g2*4 c3*4 | g2*4 g2*4 d3*4 g2*4 | f2*4 f2*4 c3*4 f2*4 | e2*4 e2*4 b2*4 e2*4

# ── BREAK — the tune goes; the bells keep watch ─────────────────────────────
section break
  bell  a5*8 .*4 c6*4 | b5*8 .*8 | c6*8 e5*4 .*4 | .*4 a5*4 .*8
        f5*8 a5*4 .*4 | g5*8 b5*4 .*4 | e5*4 g#5*4 b5*4 .*4 | .*16
  arp   f3 . a3 . c4 . a3 . f3 . a3 . c4 . a3 . | g3 . b3 . d4 . b3 . g3 . b3 . d4 . b3 . | a3 . c4 . e4 . c4 . a3 . c4 . e4 . c4 . | a3 . c4 . e4 . c4 . a3 . c4 . e4 . c4 .
        f3 . a3 . c4 . a3 . f3 . a3 . c4 . a3 . | g3 . b3 . d4 . b3 . g3 . b3 . d4 . b3 . | e3 . g#3 . b3 . g#3 . e3 . g#3 . b3 . g#3 . | e3 . g#3 . b3 . g#3 . e3 . g#3 . b3 . g#3 .
  bass  f2*8 f2*8 | g2*8 g2*8 | a2*8 a2*8 | a2*8 a2*8
        f2*8 f2*8 | g2*8 g2*8 | e2*8 e2*8 | e2*8 e2*8

section outro
  flute  e5*8 c5*4 d5*4 | c5*8 a4*8 | b4*12 .*4 | .*16
  bell   .*16 | .*16 | .*16 | e5*4 b4*4 g#4*8
  bass   a2*8 a2*8 | f2*8 f2*8 | e2*8 e2*8 | e2*16

order  intro verse chorus verse break chorus outro
